  "body": "## What changed\n- New module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/lead_seam.rs` with `seam_tangents`.\n- `lead_fit.rs` calls `seam_tangents` from `both_fit` and `plan_leads`.\n- At the seam of a closed ring, the function builds the full lead along the walk's end tangent.\n- It checks that lead against the ring's own feed moves. It uses the verifier's crossing law (`arc_cross::moves_cross_prior`).\n- Only a lead that crosses gets a new tangent: the old tangent mirrored across the other end's tangent.\n- The mirrored lead is used only if it does not cross.\n- A lead that does not cross keeps its tangent. Open walks keep their tangents.\n- New test file `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_lead.rs`.\n- Decision record `docs/decisions/3019-contour-lead-cross-only.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- On the issue's R6 plate, the seam falls on a fitted corner arc.\n- The 8 mm linear lead-out along that arc's end tangent crossed the ring's long bottom edge next to the seam. The lead-in did the same on a conventional cut.\n- Verify found one crossing on each level. Tabs are not the cause: the same crossing occurs with no tabs.\n- The first fix (#3053) mirrored the tangent on each closed ring that bent at the seam. That also changed plain rectangles with no crossing (#3111). #3114 reverted it.\n- This fix changes a lead only when that lead crosses its own ring.\n\n## Tests\nPins (120 x 80 plate, four R6 corners, D10 tool, stepdown 3, 12 deep, linear lead 8):\n- `an_outside_tabbed_contour_with_a_linear_lead_has_no_crossing` (climb, 4 tabs).\n- `an_outside_contour_with_a_linear_lead_has_no_crossing_with_or_without_tabs` (climb with 0 tabs; conventional with 0 and 4 tabs).\n- Each case asserts no `crossed_pairs`, no `Crossing` or `Gouge` from `verify`, and a full 8 mm lead-in and lead-out.\n- The regression pin of #3111 is `vertical_arc_entry` (motion and post). It is green on this head.\n\nRed before the fix: yes, both pins. Failure text: `4 tabs, climb: feed crossings [[5, 14], [21, 30], [37, 46], [53, 62]]`.\n\nMutations:\n- M1, old `lead_fit.rs` from upstream/main: both pins red.\n- M2, lead-out mirror removed: both pins red (`[[5, 14], ...]`).\n- M3, lead-in mirror removed: the conventional case red (`[[3, 12], [19, 28], [35, 44], [51, 60]]`).\n- M4, crossing check replaced by the #3053 bend law: motion `vertical_arc_entry` red (`an_oblique_first_cut_stays_chords_and_says_so_once`, `an_x_aligned_first_cut_enters_on_one_g18_arc_per_level`). This shows that the crossing check keeps other rings unchanged.\n- Fix restored: all green.\n\nGate (macOS arm64, final head `8b17c42d7f804d8409bc1ad2ddf3e3699b675815`):\n\nBase: upstream/main `f036dddad0de170aad9cd07a56ec3d53589ac517`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: PASS. All 235 gate steps passed in 27.7 minutes, including the release build.\n- Motion heavy lane: 37 target steps. 57 tests passed. The gate confirmed two expected failures tracked in #1950.\n- App heavy lane: 197 target steps. 43 tests passed. The gate confirmed four expected failures tracked in #1950 and #2849.\n- The heavy run had no unexpected failure and no ignored test. The gate ran the selected tests with `--ignored`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: PASS. Exit 0. All 133 steps passed in 23.2 minutes, including two builds. Tests: 1,612 passed, zero failed, 64 ignored. Motion: 1,047 passed and 52 ignored across 71 test steps. App: 565 passed and 12 ignored across 60 test steps.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test vertical_arc_entry`: 3/3 green in the original author checks and the review.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS. Exit 0. No warnings. Completed in 42.39 seconds.\n\nThe latest review requested heavy gate evidence only. This update changes no source or test.\nThe existing pins and mutation evidence above still apply. The review also repeated M2 and M3, then restored the fix with green results.\nThe PR remains a draft.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The QA project file of the issue (`q01-blocked.camproj`) was not opened. The pin rebuilds the same plate and operation in `camcraft-motion`.\n- Inside contours (bores) with a crossing seam lead. The check applies to them too. No pin covers them.\n- Arc and tangential leads. The check applies to each lead shape. Only the linear lead is pinned.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone. No open PR changes `lead_fit.rs`. This is a redo of #3053, which #3114 reverted.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Contour with a linear lead on a part with round corners no longer gets a lead-in or lead-out that crosses the cut at the seam, so verify does not hold the post.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3019\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
